From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] easymesh: use full client list only to seed unknown rows

The full associated-clients fallback added for startup discovery republishes
every full-map entry as a fresh association whenever the delta map is empty.
That is not snapshot reconciliation.  A client that roams without sending a
deauthentication frame can remain in an hwsim AP's station/full map while the
destination AP also reports it.  Replaying the stale entry makes the
controller alternate ownership on every refresh.

Use the full map only for its intended bootstrap purpose: seed a client that
the local EasyMesh Agent has not learned yet.  Once a same-STA/BSS/radio row is
in the Agent's consolidated map, only a real OneWifi association delta may
republish it.  Normal disassociation deltas and the returning-client refresh
path remain unchanged.

This preserves clients already present when EasyMesh starts without converting
a possibly stale platform inventory into recurring association events.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c b/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c
--- a/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c
+++ b/source/webconfig/wifi_easymesh_translator.c
@@ -1460,6 +1460,24 @@ webconfig_error_t translate_associated_clients_to_easymesh_sta_info(webconfig_su
                     proto->set_num_radio(proto->data_model, decoded_params->num_radios);
                     proto->set_num_bss(proto->data_model, radio->vaps.num_vaps);
                     printf("%s:%d: client_state: %d\n", __func__, __LINE__, assoc_dev_data->client_state);
+
+                    /* A full map is a bootstrap snapshot, not a sequence of
+                     * association deltas.  mac80211 may retain an AP station
+                     * when a roam-away is silent; replaying that entry forever
+                     * fights the destination AP's real association event. */
+                    if (em_using_full_list && vap->vap_mode == wifi_vap_mode_ap &&
+                            proto->get_sta_info(proto->data_model,
+                                assoc_dev_data->dev_stats.cli_MACAddress,
+                                vap->u.bss_info.bssid, radio_info->intf.mac,
+                                em_target_sta_map_consolidated) != NULL) {
+                        wifi_util_dbg_print(WIFI_WEBCONFIG,
+                            "%s:%d: skipping already-seeded full-list STA on vap '%s'\n",
+                            __func__, __LINE__, rdk_vap_info->vap_name);
+                        free(em_sta_dev_info);
+                        assoc_dev_data = hash_map_get_next(em_assoc_src,
+                            assoc_dev_data);
+                        continue;
+                    }
 
                     memcpy(em_sta_dev_info->id, assoc_dev_data->dev_stats.cli_MACAddress, sizeof(mac_address_t));
                     if (vap->vap_mode == wifi_vap_mode_ap) {
